This is the exact consolidated collision-safe rank screen obtained by coupling the full loaded-source selector, the \(\chi\)-centroid submeasure, and the simultaneous contact-edge measures.  It keeps the correlated lower bound for \(X/Q\) instead of replacing it by \(1/160\), and it charges \(R\), \(G\), \(R_{\rm sel}(C)\), \(M_{\rm off}(C)\), and \(D=2^nh_{\max}(C)\) exactly once.  For every affine field used in the far-support construction, every hard \(I\)-dominant configuration satisfies
\[
 \frac{2048}{11}\,
 \frac{\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_P}}{r_P+1}
 \mathbin{+}\frac{2^{n-\rho_\chi}}{r_{\bar c}+1}
 \mathbin{+}\max\left\{
  \frac{2\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_\chi}}{r_\ell+1},
  \frac{16\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_\chi}}{r_F+1},
  \frac{17\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_\chi}}{r_*+1},
  \frac{32\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_a^{\rm far}}}
       {17(r_a^{\rm far}+1)}
 \right\}
 <\frac{128}{275}.
\]
This strictly strengthens the separate source and contact screens.  It is not a final because all displayed normalized scores may still be small through large residual ranks.
